======================================================================
ATTACK 2 RESULTS
======================================================================
Variant A (single-ID pump):     gaming flagged but patterns validated
Variant B (rotated pairs):      bypassed gaming + validated 5 absurd claims
Variant C (cross-session):      persistent false claim graduated across sessions

Defense gap: graduation is per-session and per-citation. There is
no cross-session 'has this pattern actually been load-bearing in
downstream decisions?' check, and gaming detection ONLY catches the
single-ID-frequency case. Rotated-pair citation = full bypass.
